            <ArticleTitle>Use of a deflectable tip catheter to facilitate complex interventions beyond insertion of coronary bypass grafts: three case reports.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>862-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present three patients with angulated ostial lesions beyond the insertion point of coronary artery bypass grafts. Use of the Venture Catheter, a deflectable tip 3.5F wire control catheter, facilitated successful percutaneous coronary intervention after prolonged, unsuccessful attempts at conventional guidewire passage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
